        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tasks): fail closed when task-flow state cannot restore",
        "body": "Related: #71689\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where unreadable or corrupt task-flow SQLite state could appear as an empty registry while linked task commands, runtime cancellation, startup maintenance, or in-process gateway restart continued from partially restored durable state.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTask-flow restore now publishes state atomically and keeps a sticky failed state until an explicit reload succeeds. The task-owned lifecycle seam restores flow state before task state, cold startup and `SIGUSR1` restart stop before task listeners or maintenance can activate, and linked mutations/cancellation preflight every affected flow projection before runtime side effects.\n\nThe cancellation gate preserves runtime-only task ownership and still permits final terminal projections that no longer need a flow mutation.\n\n## User Impact\n\nTask and task-flow state now fails closed instead of allowing partial durable-state mutations or runtime cancellation after a restore failure. Operators can audit the preserved diagnostic, repair the database, and retry with an in-process gateway restart.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact PR head: `bb46925e6c7538d6b3846a8a920180232c25cdbc`.\n- Direct AWS Crabbox `cbx_f224f52727e4`, run `run_fa1470eda1c3`: 218 focused task, task-flow, command, and gateway tests passed on the earlier branch stack.\n- Final rebased branch: 222 focused tests passed together; cancellation-specific reruns passed 18 gateway task, 140 executor/registry, 4 boundary, and 19 command tests.\n- Fresh full-branch autoreview against current `origin/main`: clean, confidence 0.88.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: passed.\n- Interactive `pnpm check:changed` was attempted on fresh AWS and Blacksmith leases, but provider SSH/bootstrap and delegated sync failed before command execution. Exact-head hosted PR CI is the remaining broad gate.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. The final patch was inspected, focused-tested, and autoreviewed.\n",
